safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":9,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed PKT-0080's acceptance command, both PKT-0083 acceptance commands pass, and the work is committed. The second command only passes because nothing was there to check, though, and it will fail once PKT-0080 goes back to in-progress (details below).\n\n**What changed**\n- **Profiler script:** I copied `.theseus/oracle/perf/profile-fonts.js` unchanged from commit 75204fd, which was only on `pkt/PKT-0072`. No other oracle script was touched.\n- **PKT-0080 acceptance:** I replaced the literal `<samples-dir>` with `python3 .theseus/oracle/perf/make-samples.py /tmp/eo-samples && node .theseus/oracle/perf/profile-fonts.js /tmp/eo-samples external/sdkjs 3`. The command now creates the samples before profiling, so it doesn't rely on an existing `/tmp` folder. `/tmp/eo-samples` is the path earlier packets used, and `make-samples.py` always produces the same files.\n\n**Problems for the reviewer**\n- **PKT-0080 is in `queue/blocked/`, not `queue/in-progress/`** as `target.files` says. I edited the file of the same name in `blocked/`. Because no file matches the `in-progress/` path, the `! grep` command has nothing to search and passes regardless of what PKT-0080 contains.\n- **`<samples-dir>` is still in PKT-0080's Executor log, 5 times**, in lines that quote the earlier failures. The contract says the log stays as written, so I left them. Once PKT-0080 is moved back to `in-progress/`, the `! grep` command will fail on that text. The fix is to search only the acceptance block or to allow editing the log; the factory or reviewer needs to choose.\n\n**Not done:** I didn't run the profiler itself. Showing the gain needs PKT-0080's sdkjs build copied into the installed server with `sdkjs-mirror.sh`, which is outside this packet.\n\n`theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 1 warning; I didn't check what the warning is about. The Executor log and the friction line are written.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- An acceptance command must not contain `<...>` placeholders, because the shell treats `<` as an input redirect and fails before the command starts.\n- Oracle scripts must be on the base branch before a packet's acceptance can use them.\n- A `grep` check with a glob that matches no file passes without checking anything; check that the file exists first.","ttft_ms":2082,"type":"result","duration_ms":36016,"uuid":"db4309d7-6f17-4176-81fe-c2d52bf8a559","ttft_stream_ms":1010,"time_to_request_ms":508,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":380,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":5,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":29,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":22,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":103,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":214,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":194,"process_anon_mib_result":131,"process_peak_rss_mib":228,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1760,"process_wall_ms_turn":36015,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":607,"process_wall_ms_streaming":22967,"main_stream_count":9,"main_stream_event_count":543,"main_stream_chunk_count":320,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":18,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":7,"ambient_wait_ms":8,"render_ms":1,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":1010,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":4810866,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793663506106.6487,"queued_turn_count":0,"result